{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41159656",
      "title": "Configuring Dynamic Routes & Using Route Parameters",
      "lectureOrder": 93,
      "videoOrder": 86,
      "sourceHash": "326c369009887bc057eae63371188031a2cc4e4038c7ec74dedda6949838ec3b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 3.24,
          "en": "So now that we have a solid understanding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.24,
          "end": 5.52,
          "en": "of how we can generally set up routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.52,
          "end": 8.4,
          "en": "and also work with regular components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.4,
          "end": 10.47,
          "en": "before we dive into that Meals app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.47,
          "end": 13.47,
          "en": "there's just one other route type I also wanna",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.47,
          "end": 15.6,
          "en": "explore together with you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.6,
          "end": 19.47,
          "en": "Because let's say we also wanna have a blog route in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.47,
          "end": 22.95,
          "en": "So of course we could add a blog folder in the app directory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.95,
          "end": 25.14,
          "en": "and add a page.js file in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.14,
          "end": 29.01,
          "en": "But let's then say, we also wanna have different blog posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.01,
          "end": 31.65,
          "en": "So that nested in that blog folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.65,
          "end": 36.51,
          "en": "we have a post-1 folder, a post-2 folder, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.51,
          "end": 40.5,
          "en": "And of course, this then doesn't lead anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.5,
          "end": 44.49,
          "en": "because this would mean that we need to add a new folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.49,
          "end": 48.12,
          "en": "whenever a new blog post is added to the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.12,
          "end": 53.12,
          "en": "or wherever we're storing them, and that is not scalable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.13,
          "end": 54.93,
          "en": "and not maintainable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.93,
          "end": 56.34,
          "en": "So what we need here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.34,
          "end": 59.88,
          "en": "for these posts is a so-called dynamic route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.88,
          "end": 62.85,
          "en": "a route which we only define once,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.85,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "but which is then capable of rendering different pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 68.343,
          "en": "for different blog posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.57,
          "end": 73.62,
          "en": "And in NextJS, we can create such a dynamic route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.62,
          "end": 77.97,
          "en": "by adding a nested folder where we use square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.97,
          "end": 81.44200000000001,
          "en": "This is a special syntax supported by NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.44200000000001,
          "end": 85.89,
          "en": "where you then put any placeholder, any identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.89,
          "end": 89.58,
          "en": "of your choice between those square brackets, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.58,
          "end": 92.1,
          "en": "slug, or whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.1,
          "end": 95.07300000000001,
          "en": "And this placeholder will become important later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 98.85,
          "en": "Then we again, need a page.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.85,
          "end": 102.15,
          "en": "because of course we want to render some content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.15,
          "end": 103.77000000000001,
          "en": "And if you want to build a new page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.77000000000001,
          "end": 107.10300000000001,
          "en": "that should be visitable, you need a page.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.63,
          "end": 111.06,
          "en": "Now let's start with the page.js file directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.06,
          "end": 113.28,
          "en": "in the blog folder though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.28,
          "end": 117.28,
          "en": "There we could of course export a component called BlogPage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.22999999999999,
          "end": 121.92,
          "en": "where we then return this main element maybe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.92,
          "end": 123.717,
          "en": "and say, \"The Blog\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.8,
          "end": 128.13,
          "en": "And then here I want to have, let's say, two paragraphs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.13,
          "end": 130.653,
          "en": "with links to different blog posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.52,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "So I'll use that link component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 136.353,
          "en": "and import that from next/link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.64,
          "end": 141.09,
          "en": "And then here, let's say we wanna have one blog post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.09,
          "end": 142.92000000000002,
          "en": "under \"/blog/post-1\" like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.64,
          "end": 151.74,
          "en": "but then we also wanna have a second one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.74,
          "end": 156.063,
          "en": "that leads to Post 2 here in that path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.32,
          "end": 159,
          "en": "So almost the same path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159,
          "end": 161.523,
          "en": "but different segments here at the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.25,
          "end": 168.36,
          "en": "Now we need to go to that page.js file in that slug folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.36,
          "end": 170.73,
          "en": "in that square brackets slug folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.73,
          "end": 171.9,
          "en": "And here of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.9,
          "end": 174.93,
          "en": "we also should export a component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.93,
          "end": 177.903,
          "en": "the blog post page, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.33,
          "end": 182.88,
          "en": "And there we can again, return the main element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.88,
          "end": 187.413,
          "en": "and say \"Blog Post\", and we'll make this more dynamic later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.45,
          "end": 191.61,
          "en": "With that, if we save everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 191.61,
          "end": 196.57,
          "en": "and you go back, you will see that if you visit /blog,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 199.32,
          "end": 200.61,
          "en": "you have these two links,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 200.61,
          "end": 203.01,
          "en": "and if you click them, indeed you're taken",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.01,
          "end": 204.48,
          "en": "to that blog post page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 204.48,
          "end": 207.66,
          "en": "And that works for both links.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 207.66,
          "end": 210.12,
          "en": "And as you can tell, if you take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 210.12,
          "end": 213.78,
          "en": "at this URL, it changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 213.78,
          "end": 218.78,
          "en": "We have post-2 here as a segment after /blog",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 218.82,
          "end": 222.39,
          "en": "and post-1 for that other link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 222.39,
          "end": 225.6,
          "en": "But it's the same page.js file becoming active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 225.6,
          "end": 228.18,
          "en": "for different segment values, so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 228.18,
          "end": 231.42000000000002,
          "en": "for different path segment values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 231.42000000000002,
          "end": 233.1,
          "en": "And that is what is achieved with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 233.1,
          "end": 236.16,
          "en": "that dynamic route syntax here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.16,
          "end": 240.531,
          "en": "This square bracket thing here simply tells NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 240.531,
          "end": 244.23,
          "en": "that we want to have some path segment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 244.23,
          "end": 246.33,
          "en": "after blog in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 246.33,
          "end": 250.413,
          "en": "but that we don't know the exact value of the segment yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 251.49,
          "end": 255.66,
          "en": "And it's then this placeholder, this identifier slug",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 255.66,
          "end": 258.6,
          "en": "that will give us access to the concrete value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 258.6,
          "end": 262.023,
          "en": "that we do get when that route is loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 262.98,
          "end": 266.91,
          "en": "Because NextJS actually passes a props object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 266.91,
          "end": 269.52,
          "en": "to all those page components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 269.52,
          "end": 273.21,
          "en": "And all these page components get one special prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 273.21,
          "end": 276.45,
          "en": "which you can pull out with help of destructuring,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 276.45,
          "end": 280.29,
          "en": "and that's a params prop, which again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 280.29,
          "end": 282.27,
          "en": "is set by NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 282.27,
          "end": 284.31,
          "en": "You don't have to pass it manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 284.31,
          "end": 287.97,
          "en": "because you're not rendering these components manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.97,
          "end": 290.61,
          "en": "Instead, NextJS is doing that for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.61,
          "end": 293.043,
          "en": "and it is setting this prop for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 294.09000000000003,
          "end": 296.37,
          "en": "And what's inside of this params prop?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 296.37,
          "end": 298.53,
          "en": "Well, this will be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 298.53,
          "end": 303.21,
          "en": "where every placeholder you had in such a dynamic route here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 303.21,
          "end": 304.86,
          "en": "will be a key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 304.86,
          "end": 306.51,
          "en": "And the value stored under",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 306.51,
          "end": 310.113,
          "en": "that key will be the concrete value encoded in the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 310.95,
          "end": 313.833,
          "en": "So post-1, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 315.36,
          "end": 318.81,
          "en": "And you can see that if you output it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 318.81,
          "end": 322.47,
          "en": "by accessing params.slug here in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 322.47,
          "end": 323.853,
          "en": "in this page here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 325.56,
          "end": 329.67,
          "en": "If you do that, you see post-1 here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 329.67,
          "end": 334.67,
          "en": "If I enter anything-else here, you see anything-else here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 336.45,
          "end": 338.19,
          "en": "And this is a great feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 338.19,
          "end": 342.06,
          "en": "because this would now allow you to, for example, reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 342.06,
          "end": 346.23,
          "en": "to a database where your blog posts might be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 346.23,
          "end": 349.5,
          "en": "and fetch the blog post with that slug so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 349.5,
          "end": 352.83299999999997,
          "en": "that you can then show its content on this page instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 353.85,
          "end": 357.45,
          "en": "And that's how you can set up such dynamic routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 357.45,
          "end": 360.54,
          "en": "Now, NextJS has way more to offer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 360.54,
          "end": 364.05,
          "en": "You can also set up custom not found pages, deal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 364.05,
          "end": 368.49,
          "en": "with errors, add more pages, fetch data, change data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 368.49,
          "end": 371.88,
          "en": "and we'll do all that, but not in this demo project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 371.88,
          "end": 375.453,
          "en": "Instead by working on that Meals app I showed you before.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
